# Chef’s Mind AI — UI Specification v1  
_Final approved UI structure._

---

## 0. Core UI Principles

- Dark, minimalist, fine-dining fusion aesthetic (June Six style).  
- Universal Chat is the **main entry point** (home).  
- Left sidebar = agent workspaces.  
- Right sidebar = tools (calendar, search, media library, DB outline).  
- Universal Chat and Agent Chats must always be visually distinct via  
  **a large, explicit header at the top**.

---

# 1. Login Screen

**Displayed only when the user is not authenticated.**

### Structure:

- Fullscreen layout with **no sidebars**.
- Background: dimmed hero image (e.g. `login-hero-chefs-mind-ai.jpg`)  
  — dark kitchen, soft side light, Na’Vi blue accent.
- Center (or left column):
  - Logo: `Chef’s Mind AI`
  - Subtitle:  
    _AI assistant for kitchen, accounting and media_
  - Primary button:  
    **Sign in with Google** → `/auth/google`
  - Optional footer text:  
    _Access restricted to the owner and June Six team._

### Behavior:

- First Google login = registration.  
- No username/password forms.  
- Logout is available via profile menu after login.

---

# 2. Main Application Shell (after login)

Visible immediately after successful authentication:

- **Left Sidebar** (navigation & workspaces)
- **Central Area** (chats / agent workspaces)
- **Right Sidebar** (tools & utilities)
- **Header**:
  - Optional small logo on the left
  - User avatar on the right (Profile / Logout)

---

# 3. Universal Chat (Home)

### Opened when:
- Logging in for the first time  
- Clicking the **Chef’s Mind AI logo** in the left sidebar  
- Clicking **`+ New Chat`**

### Header:
**Universal Chat**  
(large, top-aligned)

### Behavior:
- Uses the **Orchestrator** to route requests to Chef / Accountant / Researcher / Media.  
- Can also operate with a manually selected agent/model.  
- Input area:
  - text field
  - send button
  - file attachment
  - (optional) agent/model selector

### Purpose:
Your primary “GPT-style” interaction space.

---

# 4. Left Sidebar — Final Structure

**From top to bottom:**

### 4.1 Logo / Home
- Clickable `Chef’s Mind AI`  
- Returns to **Universal Chat**

### 4.2 New Universal Chat
- Button: **`+ New Chat`**  
- Creates a new **Universal Chat** (orchestrator)

### 4.3 Agent Workspaces
- `Chef`  
- `Accountant`  
- `Researcher`  
- `Media Studio`  

Clicking any agent opens its dedicated workspace.

### 4.4 Bottom Section
- **⚙ Settings** — always located at the very bottom

### Rules:
- **Universal Chat does NOT appear as an item** in the sidebar.  
- **QA agent is never shown** (internal system layer).

---

# 5. Agent Workspaces  
(Chef / Accountant / Researcher / Media Studio)

Each agent has its own “project-like” workspace.

### Central layout:

#### Left column (inside central area):
- List of chats belonging to this agent:
  - chat title/ID  
  - timestamp  
- Button: **`+ New Chat`** (for this specific agent)

#### Right column:
- **Large header** (e.g. `Chef — Chat #12`)  
- Agent badge / icon  
- Message history  
- Input area  
- File attachments  
- (optional) per-chat settings

---

# 6. Media Studio — Special Features

Media Studio is treated as an **agent workspace**, but with extended UI.

### Additional elements in the chat panel:

- Task type selector:  
  - `Image` / `Video`
- Model selector:  
  - `DALL·E`  
  - `Imagen`  
  - `Veo`
- Generation parameters (resolution, duration, etc.)
- **Add Reference** button:
  - upload reference image or short video
  - list of references displayed above input or in a sidebar

**Note:**  
Media generation can also be initiated from **Universal Chat**;  
Media Studio provides a more structured workflow.

---

# 7. Right Sidebar — Final Structure

A universal collapsible sidebar available on all screens.

## 7.1 Search
- Search across:
  - chats  
  - (optional) media  
  - (future) notes  

## 7.2 Media Library
- Stream of image/video previews  
- Metadata:  
  - timestamp  
  - model  
  - agent origin  
- Click → fullscreen overlay (preview + prompt + parameters)

## 7.3 DB Outline
Light-weight overview of key entities:
- Orders  
- Suppliers  
- Calendar Events  
- Notes  
(No CRUD in v1 — overview only)

## 7.4 Agent Status
- Active agent for the current chat  
- Last routing actions (e.g. “routed to Media → DALL·E”)  
- Status: idle / thinking / error

## 7.5 Calendar Button (Overlay)
- Icon: **📅 Calendar**
- Opens a **global overlay calendar**, not a page

### Calendar Overlay:
- Monthly grid view  
- Navigation:
  - `←` previous month  
  - `→` next month  
  - `Today`
- Highlighted dates with events  
- Clicking a day → right side of the overlay shows:
  - events  
  - times  
  - notes (order, reservation, meeting)

**The Calendar is NOT an agent and NOT a page — it is a tool.**

---

# 8. Settings Page

Accessible from **⚙ Settings** in the lower-left sidebar.

### Includes:

### 8.1 Profile
- Google email  
- Logout

### 8.2 Models & Providers
- Enabled providers (OpenAI, Google, Perplexity, etc.)  
- Default model/agent for Universal Chat

### 8.3 Appearance
- Dark theme (default)  
- Accent color (Na’Vi blue)

### 8.4 Safety
- SAFE_MODE (on/off)  
- Confirmations for sensitive operations  
  (backup, import, destructive DB tasks)

---

# 9. Avoiding Confusion Between Universal & Agent Chats

To ensure clarity:

- Every chat (Universal or Agent) has a **very large header**:
  - `Universal Chat`
  - `Chef`
  - `Media Studio`
  - etc.
- Optional color badges / icons per agent

This removes all ambiguity.

---

# 10. Extensibility (For Future Versions)

Potential improvements:

- Tabbed right sidebar (to reduce clutter)  
- DB viewer with editable tables  
- Extended Media Studio modes  
- Supplier & inventory integrations  
- Workspace templates (chat presets for events/projects)

---

# End of file  
_This document defines the agreed-upon UI foundation for Chef’s Mind AI._
